{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"List projects"},"description":"List the projects of the workspace, newest first, at most 100 per page. A project is any tracked business object with a name, a kind and a status: deal, pipeline, pipeline_stage, cost_center, property, project, campaign, audience, flow, ad. Each row gives its project_id, name, kind, status, dates, amount and currency, the project it nests under (parent_project_id), for a deal its stage_project_id and stage_name (both null when unstaged), owner_person_id, counterparty_company_id or counterparty_person_id, probability (a percentage) and position, for a project its billing_method (project_rate, service_rate, person_rate, fixed_fee, non_billable, or null when none is stated), and whether a connected tool synced it in (`synced`: Well neither deletes such a project nor changes the fields that tool writes), plus its provenance (`well` unless a connector wrote the row or the stage whose name it embeds, in which case it is `connector`). Pipelines and their stages are projects too: list kind pipeline, then kind pipeline_stage, to find the stage a deal sits on.\n\nUse it to answer \"which deals are open?\", \"which stage is this deal in?\" or \"list my campaigns\", and to find the project_id that well_update_project and well_delete_project take. A row's dates are not its history: for what changed on a project or deal, and when, pass its project_id to well_list_project_changes, which reads the changes Well recorded. Filter with kind or status. Page with `cursor` from the previous result's `next_cursor`. It reads projects, not the workspace's customers: use well_list_customers for the companies it sells to.\n\nA first-page call with kind `deal` or no kind also returns exact open-deal totals, separate by currency, with a per-workspace block and the largest eligible deal in each currency. `scope` defaults to `this_workspace`; pass `all_my_workspaces` when the person asks across their workspaces. That scope reads only the live real-workspace set authorized for this call, keeps guest project sharing in each workspace, and counts no deal twice across different workspace records. No currency conversion is applied. Global totals are null when a workspace read fails, hits a row limit or is omitted; per-workspace subtotals remain labeled with their read state. The project page and its cursor stay independent of these totals; a call with `cursor` or another kind returns the page alone.\n\nWhen the token authorizes one workspace, call this directly \u2014 no workspace call is needed first. When it authorizes several, this read will not guess which one you mean: pass `workspace_id` on the call.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"conversation_id":{"description":"The conversation id returned by the previous Well result, in its meta under well/conversation_id, in its structuredContent, or in its JSON text block. Pass it back on every call in the same conversation, including a call a card makes, so the chosen workspace and the earlier answers still apply. It decides the conversation on its own: nothing the host states about the session replaces it. Omit it only on the first call of a conversation.","type":"string"},"cursor":{"description":"The next_cursor of the previous page.","format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$","type":"string"},"kind":{"description":"Only the projects of this kind: deal, pipeline, pipeline_stage, cost_center, property, project, campaign, audience, flow, ad.","enum":["campaign","ad","audience","flow","deal","cost_center","project","property","pipeline","pipeline_stage"],"type":"string"},"limit":{"description":"Rows to return, at most 100. Default 20.","maximum":100,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"scope":{"description":"Measure this workspace only or all_my_workspaces across the authorized real workspaces of the signed-in person.","enum":["this_workspace","all_my_workspaces"],"type":"string"},"status":{"description":"Only the projects in this status: draft, active, paused, won, lost, archived, completed.","enum":["draft","active","paused","won","lost","completed","archived"],"type":"string"},"workspace_id":{"description":"Target workspace. Omit when the token authorizes one workspace. Required when it authorizes several: this read reports one workspace's own figures and will not choose which.","format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$","type":"string"},"workspace_scope":{"description":"Restrict this call to the family: the token's primary workspace plus the company workspaces under it that you are a member of. Unrelated authorized workspaces drop out of the read; row reads merge across the family, while a per-workspace figure still reports exactly one workspace.","enum":["family"],"type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"well_list_projects","outputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"all_workspaces_totals":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"currency":{"enum":["USD","EUR","GBP","JPY","CHF","CAD","AUD","NZD","SEK","NOK","DKK","PLN","CZK","HUF","RON","BGN","HRK","ISK","ALL","BAM","BYN","MDL","MKD","RSD","FOK","GGP","GIP","IMP","JEP","CNY","CNH","KRW","SGD","HKD","TWD","THB","MYR","IDR","PHP","VND","INR","PKR","LKR","BDT","BND","BTN","KHR","LAK","MMK","MNT","MOP","MVR","NPR","KID","AED","SAR","QAR","KWD","BHD","OMR","JOD","ILS","EGP","ZAR","NGN","KES","GHS","MAD","TND","DZD","CVE","GMD","GNF","LRD","MGA","MRU","SHP","SLE","SLL","SSP","STN","YER","MXN","BRL","ARS","CLP